in for David Pakman, and this is the David

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:10.530
Pakman Show, we've got all kinds of great
stuff coming up today, the latest on Afghanistan,

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:16.440
of course, some covid updates for you and
even a little bit of insight into what is

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:22.690
happening with Republican Congressman Matt
Gates and that investigation and some other

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:27.480
problems that he's having right here where
I'm sitting in Florida's 1st Congressional

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:28.480
District.

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:30.199
But let's kick things off.

00:00:30.199 --> 00:00:35.680
Obviously, still the biggest news in the world
right now, Afghanistan.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:38.950
Things getting worse, of course.

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:41.050
And here's something interesting that's happened.

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:46.719
And this was actually pointed out by Dave
Weigel of The Washington Post, where Weigel

00:00:46.719 --> 00:00:53.650
pointed out over the weekend that a Web page
on the RNC official website seems to have

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:54.650
disappeared.

00:00:54.650 --> 00:01:00.629
And that Web site or Web page, I guess, was
the page talking about Donald Trump's historic

00:01:00.629 --> 00:01:06.990
peace deal, as they called it, with the Taliban
with regards to Afghanistan.

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:13.249
If you go to that page now, there's just a
404 page not found error because apparently

00:01:13.249 --> 00:01:18.289
the Republican National Committee doesn't
want people seeing that they're promoting

00:01:18.289 --> 00:01:23.789
that ridiculous peace deal that Donald Trump
allegedly worked out.

00:01:23.789 --> 00:01:25.229
And there's a couple of reasons for that,
too.

00:01:25.229 --> 00:01:26.849
So let's dove right into those.

00:01:26.849 --> 00:01:32.729
First and foremost, they don't want any attention
on what Donald Trump did as president with

00:01:32.729 --> 00:01:34.599
regard to Afghanistan.

00:01:34.599 --> 00:01:39.859
And let's be honest, there's a lot but the
peace deal that he allegedly had worked out

00:01:39.859 --> 00:01:44.859
with the Taliban that was signed in February
of twenty twenty is the biggest thing they

00:01:44.859 --> 00:01:46.899
don't want people to remember.

00:01:46.899 --> 00:01:52.369
And that's because once you dig down into
the details of this so-called peace deal,

00:01:52.369 --> 00:01:54.719
you realize how horrible it actually was.

00:01:54.719 --> 00:02:01.369
And the biggest problem with this peace deal
is that it completely excluded.

00:02:01.369 --> 00:02:03.889
The Afghan government.

00:02:03.889 --> 00:02:08.829
No leaders from Afghanistan were involved
in the drafting of this and the protections

00:02:08.829 --> 00:02:14.840
that the United States agreed to with the
Taliban did not extend.

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:18.870
To the actual Afghanistan government.

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:27.819
The deal only pertained to U.S. troops and
our NATO allies in the country that the Taliban

00:02:27.819 --> 00:02:33.680
would not attack them in exchange for the
United States agreeing to leave the country

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:36.159
within 14 months.

00:02:36.159 --> 00:02:43.159
But nowhere, not any part of that agreement
did the Taliban say, oh, by the way, we won't

00:02:43.159 --> 00:02:47.470
promise to not attack the Afghanistan government.

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:51.689
Apparently, that was just a major oversight.

00:02:51.689 --> 00:02:58.640
Of this peace deal and of course, as soon
as the United States leaves, the Taliban goes

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:01.780
and overthrows the government of Afghanistan.

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:09.950
So, yeah, it's not surprising that they would
want that Web page removed from existence

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:13.790
because they're boasting about it, talking
about, look what Donald Trump did, bringing

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:18.010
peace to the Middle East with this historic
deal.

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:23.849
Nope, nope, another total failure by Donald
Trump.

00:03:23.849 --> 00:03:27.980
Another reason, though, that they do not want
this page out there in existence and I think

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:34.170
this is probably the bigger one, is because
they want all the focus right now to be on

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:36.590
Joe Biden.

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:41.430
That is the goal, make this Biden's failure.

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:48.120
Make this all about his decision to remove
Trump from our troops from Afghanistan, ignoring

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:52.469
the fact that even just a couple months ago,
Donald Trump was, you know, screaming at the

00:03:52.469 --> 00:03:58.550
top of his lungs to tell Joe Biden to get
the troops out of Afghanistan.

00:03:58.550 --> 00:04:04.760
But they have to frame this as Biden's failure,
because that's the new talking point in immerge

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:10.110
fast, it emerged quick and based on what we're
seeing in the media, tends to be the sticking

00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:15.650
narrative at this point that this is all Joe
Biden's fault.

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:20.370
And let's obviously be clear about this, that's
not the case.

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:25.789
This is the fault of four different administrations,
but if you had to lay the blame at anybody's

00:04:25.789 --> 00:04:29.250
feet, that blame is going to be squarely at
the feet of George W. Bush.

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:31.870
And I will get more into that in just a little
bit.

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:39.810
But the talking point from the RNC, from Republican
officials, from elected officials, from Donald

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:46.870
Trump himself, is all about Joe Biden being
a catastrophic failure and they're hoping

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:50.240
that they can ride this all the way through
the midterms.

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:54.550
You know, I pointed out yesterday on the program
that the Republicans have had a hell of a

00:04:54.550 --> 00:04:57.990
time getting any kind of talking point to
stick about.

00:04:57.990 --> 00:04:59.639
Joe Biden.

00:04:59.639 --> 00:05:01.340
They have crafted all these narratives.

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:03.319
Fox News has tested them out.

00:05:03.319 --> 00:05:06.950
And even Fox News at one point was getting
frustrated because nothing they were saying

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:11.360
or using to attack Biden was resonating with
the audience.

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:14.150
Well, this is something that would resonate.

00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:20.060
And again, as I mentioned, fair or not, Biden
was the president when this happened.

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:25.440
So if people are going to blame somebody,
they are going to blame him.

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:30.009
I don't agree with that assessment at all,
but I also live in reality.

00:05:30.009 --> 00:05:34.991
I've been doing this long enough, you know,
coming up on two decades at this point, we

00:05:34.991 --> 00:05:37.449
know how these things play out.

00:05:37.449 --> 00:05:42.150
We know where the blame is going to go and
we know the talking points that the Republicans

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:45.160
are going to use.

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:48.639
And one of the main reasons we know that is
because we're literally already seeing it

00:05:48.639 --> 00:05:53.289
